(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "cloud-itonami-isic-5911 scope extension to AI-generated/SNS-native video production" "closed decision not to open a new ISIC repo for Higgsfield/Tripo-style viral-video AI generation + posting support")), (:adr/topic "cloud-itonami-isic-5911-viral-social-video-scope"), (:adr/related (vector "ADR-2620100000" "cloud-itonami-isic-5912" "cloud-itonami-isic-5913" "cloud-itonami-isic-5914" "cloud-itonami-isic-7310" "cloud-itonami-isic-5820" "cloud-itonami-isic-6201" "cloud-itonami-isic-6202" "cloud-itonami-isic-6312" "cloud-itonami-isic-6311")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2800002000-cloud-itonami-isic-5911-viral-social-video-scope"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-19"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2800002000: cloud-itonami-isic-5911 -- extend scope to AI-generated, SNS-native (\"viral video\") production, no new repo\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-19\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)\n**Related**: ADR-2620100000 (original `cloud-itonami-isic-5911` fresh\nscaffold), `cloud-itonami-isic-5912`/`5913`/`5914` (Motion Picture\ndivision siblings: post-production/distribution/projection),\n`cloud-itonami-isic-7310` (advertising), `cloud-itonami-isic-5820`\n(software publishing), `cloud-itonami-isic-6201`/`6202` (computer\nprogramming), `cloud-itonami-isic-6312`/`6311` (web portals/data\nprocessing)\n\n## Context\n\nThe repository owner asked for functionality under `cloud-itonami`\ncomparable to Higgsfield/Tripo-style viral-video AI generation and\nposting-support tooling (text-to-video/image-to-video AI generation\nservices whose output is distributed to social platforms). Before\nbuilding anything, the video-production-adjacent and posting-adjacent\nISIC Rev.4 classes were audited for an open slot: motion-picture/video/\nTV-programme production (5911), post-production (5912), distribution\n(5913), projection (5914), advertising (7310), software publishing\n(5820), computer programming (6201/6202), web portals (6312), and data\nprocessing (6311) were all confirmed **already implemented** as\n`cloud-itonami` actors -- there is no unclaimed ISIC class matching this\nrequest. Given that, the owner was presented with the option to extend\nan existing actor rather than force a new registration, and chose to\nextend `cloud-itonami-isic-5911` (motion-picture/video/TV-programme\nproduction) as the first-choice target: an AI-generation service\nproducing SNS-native video content is, functionally, a production\ncompany whose \"production\" is AI-generated and whose \"release\" is a\nsocial-platform post rather than a theatrical/broadcast release -- the\nsame operations-coordination shape `cloud-itonami-isic-5911` already\nimplements (proposal -> advise -> govern -> decide ->\ncommit|hold|escalate, coordination only, never a finalization/execution\nauthority) applies unchanged.\n\n\"Posting support\" here means coordination of the *handoff* to a\ndistribution channel (delivery manifest, chain-of-custody note) --\nnever the actual posting/publish execution, account authentication,\ncontent-moderation ruling, or monetization-eligibility determination.\nThose remain outside this actor entirely, on the same \"coordination\nonly, never a finalization/execution authority\" discipline the actor\nalready applies to on-set safety-clearance decisions.\n\n## Decision\n\nExtend `cloud-itonami-isic-5911`'s existing `filmprodops` namespace\nin place (no new repository, no new ISIC registration) with two new\nclosed-allowlist proposal ops, added symmetrically across\n`filmprodops.advisor`/`filmprodops.governor`/`filmprodops.phase` and\ntheir test suites, mirroring the existing four ops' patterns exactly:\n\n1. **`:coordinate-social-distribution-handoff`** (mirrors\n   `:coordinate-post-production-handoff`) -- drafts a completed-\n   production-asset handoff coordination to an SNS/platform\n   distribution channel (TikTok/YouTube Shorts/Instagram Reels etc.):\n   delivery manifest, chain-of-custody note. `:effect` always\n   `:propose`. Final wording of the default proposal's rationale:\n   \"完成したプロダクション成果物をSNS配信チャネルへ引き渡すための調整のみ。\n   実際の配信実行・モデレーション結果の判断・収益化の可否判断・開示表示の\n   要否判断はこのアクターの範囲外で人間が行う。\" Placed in\n   `filmprodops.phase`'s Phase 2 (`:writes`, approval-gated) and Phase 3\n   (`:auto`, governor-clean auto-commit), the same phase placement as\n   `:coordinate-post-production-handoff`.\n2. **`:flag-platform-content-policy-concern`** (mirrors\n   `:flag-onset-safety-concern`) -- surfaces a platform content-policy\n   risk (community-guideline risk, monetization-eligibility risk,\n   copyright/IP risk, AI-generated-content disclosure-labeling\n   obligation) for HUMAN triage only. `:effect` always `:propose`,\n   added to `always-escalate-ops` -- ALWAYS escalates, regardless of\n   confidence, and is permanently absent from every phase's `:auto`\n   set (same structural treatment as `:flag-onset-safety-concern`,\n   never a rollout milestone still to come). Final wording of the\n   default proposal's rationale: \"プラットフォームのコンテンツポリシー上の\n   リスク観察を報告するのみ。モデレーション・収益化・開示表示に関する最終\n   判断は必ず人間が行う。\"\n\n`filmprodops.governor`'s closed op allowlist grows from four ops to\nsix; `scope-excluded-terms` gains four new HARD, PERMANENT,\nun-overridable items -- folded into the existing unconditional\nscope-exclusion check (no new check type), phrased as the\nfinalization/execution ACTION per this fleet's established\nself-tripping-bug discipline (ADR-2620100000's \"scope-exclusion\nphrasing discipline\" note, independently re-applied here rather than\nrediscovered by trial and error):\n\n- finalizing/executing an actual platform posting or publish action\n  (e.g. `\"finalize the platform posting\"`, `\"execute the platform\n  post\"`, `\"プラットフォームへの投稿を確定\"`)\n- finalizing a content-moderation ruling (e.g. `\"finalize the content\n  moderation ruling\"`, `\"コンテンツモデレーションの合否判定を確定\"`)\n- finalizing a monetization-eligibility determination (e.g.\n  `\"finalize monetization eligibility\"`, `\"収益化適格性の判定を確定\"`)\n- waiving or bypassing an AI-generated-content disclosure obligation\n  (e.g. `\"waive the ai-generated content disclosure requirement\"`,\n  `\"ai生成コンテンツの開示表示義務を無効化\"` -- deliberately ASCII\n  lower-case `\"ai\"`, matching `text-blob`'s lower-casing of the whole\n  scanned blob before the substring scan; an upper-case `\"AI\"` term\n  would silently never match)\n\n`default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip` (the fleet's standard\nself-trip regression guard) was extended to also exercise both new\nops' own default proposal text against every demo production, and a\nparallel `legitimate-platform-content-policy-concern-is-not-scope-\nexcluded` test (mirroring the existing on-set-safety-concern one) was\nadded confirming a genuine content-policy-risk *observation* never\ntrips the block that exists to catch a *finalization* attempt.\n\n`README.md`'s Scope, Features (allowlist + HARD-checks bullets),\nStaged-rollout, and CRITICAL-safety-guardrail sections were updated to\ndescribe the six-op allowlist and the four new scope-exclusion items.\n`blueprint.edn` was left unchanged -- its `:itonami.blueprint/*`\nmetadata (domain, social-impact axes, required-technologies) remains\nsemantically accurate for this scope extension, no precedent among\nsibling actors for touching it on an in-place scope extension of this\nkind was found, and doing so was out of this change's scope.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-5911`, fresh `git worktree` outside the shared\n  checkout (per this superproject's mandatory worktree-per-agent\n  discipline), sibling `orgs/kotoba-lang/langgraph`/`langchain`\n  symlinked in so the `:dev` alias's `:local/root` overrides resolve:\n  `clojure -M:dev:test` -- raw final line: `Ran 56 tests containing\n  178 assertions.` / `0 failures, 0 errors.` (up from the pre-change\n  `41 tests containing 129 assertions` recorded in ADR-2620100000; net\n  +15 tests / +49 assertions across `advisor_test.clj`/\n  `governor_test.clj`/`phase_test.clj`/`governor_contract_test.clj`;\n  `store_contract_test.clj` confirmed unchanged -- it does not\n  restrict production types to a closed set, so no edit was needed\n  there).\n- `clojure -M:lint` -- `linting took 3591ms, errors: 0, warnings: 0`.\n- `clojure -M:dev -e \"(require 'filmprodops.sim) (filmprodops.sim/-main)\"`\n  -- exit code 0, no exceptions in output (the pre-existing demo\n  narrative was left as-is, covering the original four ops end-to-end;\n  the two new ops are exercised by the extended test suites above\n  rather than the demo script, which this change did not touch).\n- Landed via `git worktree` outside the shared `orgs/cloud-itonami/\n  cloud-itonami-isic-5911` checkout, feature branch\n  `feat/viral-social-video-scope`, pushed and merged to `main` via a\n  server-side merge (`gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5911/merges`,\n  no local merge/rebase), merge commit\n  `a8f839dbfe5b5470613079f637d7a28324293053` (parents\n  `2b5c5aa4040415e4fcc98d115496127c2bdf70f5` and\n  `a086c0aea2f5f9aa382eda0de8d282e95504d6ca`), GPG-verified. `main`\n  confirmed at no drift before push (fetched immediately before\n  pushing; `origin/main` unchanged at `2b5c5aa` throughout). Worktree,\n  local branch, and remote branch all cleaned up after the merge\n  landed.\n\n## Consequences\n\n(+) Closes the Higgsfield/Tripo-style \"AI-generated viral video +\nposting support\" gap the owner asked about, via a minimal, disciplined\nin-place extension of an existing, already-audited actor rather than\nopening an eleventh near-duplicate `cloud-itonami` repo for a slice of\nscope that structurally belongs to 5911's existing production-\noperations-coordination shape.\n\n(+) The actor's existing structural safety guarantee -- coordination\nonly, never a finalization/execution authority -- extends unchanged\nto the new scope: this actor will never finalize an actual platform\npost, a content-moderation ruling, or a monetization-eligibility\ndetermination, on the same unconditional, un-overridable governor\ndiscipline it already applies to on-set safety-clearance decisions and\nminor-performer work-hour limits.\n\n(+) Zero new repos, zero new ISIC registrations, zero new governor\ncheck *types* -- the four new exclusions folded into the existing\n`scope-exclusion-violations` check, keeping the \"three HARD checks\"\narchitecture intact.\n\n(-) Still a simulation/proposal layer, not a real platform-posting or\nAI-generation-orchestration system. This actor does not generate video\ncontent, does not select or invoke an AI generation model, does not\nauthenticate to or call any social-platform API, and does not make any\nmoderation or monetization determination -- all of that remains either\nhuman-/platform-side, or (for the actual generation step) a distinct,\nnot-yet-built concern outside this actor's operations-coordination\ncharter.\n\n(-) No integration with any real social-platform API (TikTok/YouTube/\nInstagram content or analytics APIs), matching every prior sibling\nactor's own stated standalone-blueprint limitation.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Option | Verdict | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| Open a new dedicated `cloud-itonami` repo for \"viral AI video\" | ❌ | No unclaimed ISIC class fits this exact scope (5911/5912/5913/5914/7310/5820/6201/6202/6312/6311 all already implemented); a new repo would duplicate the store/advisor/governor/phase pattern `cloud-itonami-isic-5911` already provides for exactly this domain |\n| Let the actor also draft/select AI-generation prompts or invoke a generation model directly | ❌ | Out of scope for an operations-*coordination* actor; content generation is a distinct concern from coordinating the handoff of already-produced footage, and blurring it would erode the advisor/governor boundary this fleet keeps deliberately clean |\n| Let the actor finalize the actual platform posting directly (skip escalation) for lower latency | ❌ | Directly the same fleet-wide guardrail this actor already applies to on-set safety: an operations-coordination actor never finalizes an execution/authority decision, permanently, regardless of confidence -- extended unchanged to platform posting/moderation/monetization/disclosure |\n| Phrase the four new scope-exclusion terms as bare nouns (\"platform\", \"moderation\", \"AI\") for brevity | ❌ | The exact fleet-known self-tripping-bug class documented in ADR-2620100000: a bare noun would collide with the advisor's own legitimate default rationale/summary text (which must be free to say \"SNS配信\" or \"モデレーション\" when describing its own in-scope proposal); avoided from the start via ACTION-phrased terms plus an extended self-trip regression test, not discovered via a failing test |\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2620100000 (original `cloud-itonami-isic-5911` fresh scaffold,\n  motion-picture-production-coverage -- the module shape and\n  scope-exclusion-phrasing discipline this change re-applies)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-5912`/`5913`/`5914` (Motion Picture division\n  siblings: post-production/distribution/projection, confirmed already\n  implemented during this change's scope audit)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-7310`/`5820`/`6201`/`6202`/`6312`/`6311`\n  (advertising/software-publishing/computer-programming/web-portal/\n  data-processing classes, all confirmed already implemented)\n- `filmprodops.governor/scope-excluded-terms` (this fleet's\n  finalization/execution-ACTION phrasing discipline for scope\n  exclusions)\n"), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/date "2026-07-19"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2800002000: cloud-itonami-isic-5911 -- extend scope to AI-generated, SNS-native (\"viral video\") production, no new repo"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))